\title{silverback: Tidy 'Gorilla' Experiment Builder Exports}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Reads the data files downloaded from the 'Gorilla' Experiment Builder \url{https://gorilla.sc/} and turns them into tidy tibbles. Files from Task Builder 1 and 2 and from Questionnaire Builder 1 and 2 can be read together, whether they were downloaded as one file per node or as combined files, and from several versions of an experiment. Task data are reduced to one row per response with the same columns for both task builders. Questionnaire answers are returned with one row per participant, and participant information such as status, device, randomiser outcomes and stored values is collected in one table. A summary and a set of checks point out incomplete or repeated participation and unusual response patterns before the analysis. The tables can be saved as CSV files for use in other software.
}
